{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WpqazmBnKkV1KvmTTisgg","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→{\n     2→  \"metadata\": {\n     3→    \"title\": \"Masque of the Red Death - Poe\",\n     4→    \"author\": \"Edgar Allan Poe\",\n     5→    \"source_file\": \"Test_Texts/Masque of the Red Death - Poe.txt\",\n     6→    \"source_format\": \"txt\",\n     7→    \"total_word_count\": 2449,\n     8→    \"total_character_count\": 13811,\n     9→    \"estimated_total_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    10→    \"words_per_minute\": 150\n    11→  },\n    12→  \"structure\": [\n    13→    {\n    14→      \"type\": \"chapter\",\n    15→      \"title\": null,\n    16→      \"index\": 1,\n    17→      \"start_position\": 28,\n    18→      \"end_position\": 13811,\n    19→      \"word_count\": 2443,\n    20→      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n    21→      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n    22→      \"children\": [],\n    23→      \"characters_present\": [\n    24→        \"Prince Prospero\",\n    25→        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n    26→      ],\n    27→      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the Red Death, a fatal plague marked by bleeding pores and scarlet stains that isolates victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, fortified abbey, where he provides endless entertainment and provisions, sealing themselves off from the outside world. Months later, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread. During the midnight chime, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through the seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse and die upon confronting it in the black chamber — revealing the figure to be the plague incarnate, which then claims every reveller as darkness and decay consume the abbey.\"\n    28→    }\n    29→  ],\n    30→  \"characters\": [\n    31→    {\n    32→      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n    33→      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n    34→      \"aliases\": [\n    35→        \"the mummer\"\n    36→      ],\n    37→      \"role\": null,\n    38→      \"appearance\": null,\n    39→      \"personality\": null,\n    40→      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n    41→      \"descriptions\": [\n    42→        {\n    43→          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a tyrannical and self-indulgent ruler who prioritizes his own pleasure and power over the lives of others. His actions—such as ordering the execution of a masked figure and reacting with rage and cowardice when confronted—reveal a character driven by fear, arrogance, and cruelty, ultimately leading to his own demise.\",\n    44→          \"source_position\": 10339,\n    45→          \"chapter_index\": null,\n    46→          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n    47→        }\n    48→      ],\n    49→      \"relationships\": {},\n    50→      \"evidence\": [\n    51→        {\n    52→          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero demands the execution of the masked figure, calling him a blasphemer\",\n    53→          \"quote\": \"Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n    54→          \"position\": 11148,\n    55→          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n    56→        },\n    57→        {\n    58→          \"statement\": \"He is described as bold and robust, indicating physical and psychological dominance\",\n    59→          \"quote\": \"the prince was a bold and robust man\",\n    60→          \"position\": 11148,\n    61→          \"confidence\":