on\": 28,\n      \"end_position\": 13811,\n      \"word_count\": 2443,\n      \"estimated_duration_minutes\": 16.286666666666665,\n      \"confidence\": \"medium\",\n      \"children\": [],\n      \"characters_present\": [\n        \"Prince Prospero\",\n        \"The masked figure (Red Death)\"\n      ],\n      \"summary\": \"The chapter opens with the devastating spread of the Red Death, a fatal plague marked by bleeding pores and scarlet stains that isolates victims from society. Prince Prospero, in defiance of the plague, retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, fortified abbey, where he provides endless entertainment and provisions, sealing themselves off from the outside world. Months later, he hosts a lavish masked ball in seven uniquely colored rooms, each with stained-glass windows matching their hue, culminating in a black chamber with blood-red panes and a massive ebony clock that chimes hourly, halting the festivities and instilling dread. During the midnight chime, a mysterious figure appears dressed as the Red Death itself, drenched in blood and wearing a corpse-like mask, causing terror and paralysis among the guests. Prince Prospero, enraged, pursues the figure through the seven rooms with a dagger, only to collapse and die upon confronting it in the black chamber — revealing the figure to be the plague incarnate, which then claims every reveller as darkness and decay consume the abbey.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"char_the_prince_prospero_d85685e9\",\n      \"canonical_name\": \"the Prince Prospero\",\n      \"aliases\": [\n        \"the mummer\"\n      ],\n      \"role\": null,\n      \"appearance\": null,\n      \"personality\": null,\n      \"voice_guidance\": null,\n      \"descriptions\": [\n        {\n          \"text\": \"Prince Prospero is a tyrannical and self-indulgent ruler who prioritizes his own pleasure and power over the lives of others. His actions—such as ordering the execution of a masked figure and reacting with rage and cowardice when confronted—reveal a character driven by fear, arrogance, and cruelty, ultimately leading to his own demise.\",\n          \"source_position\": 10339,\n          \"chapter_index\": null,\n          \"confidence\": \"llm_refined\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"relationships\": {},\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"Prince Prospero demands the execution of the masked figure, calling him a blasphemer\",\n          \"quote\": \"Seize him and unmask him -- that we may know whom we have to hang at sunrise, from the battlements!\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is described as bold and robust, indicating physical and psychological dominance\",\n          \"quote\": \"the prince was a bold and robust man\",\n          \"position\": 11148,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He rushes forward in rage and fear, showing a loss of composure and cowardice\",\n          \"quote\": \"the Prince Prospero, maddening with rage and the shame of his own momentary cowardice, rushed hurriedly through the six chambers\",\n          \"position\": 12389,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"He is killed by the masked figure, who is revealed to be the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"the dagger dropped gleaming upon the sable carpet, upon which, instantly afterwards, fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\",\n          \"position\": 12980,\n          \"confidence\": \"high\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"statement\": \"The masked figure is revealed to be wearing grave cerements and a corpse-like mask, symbolizing the Red Death\",\n          \"quote\": \"gasped in unutterable horror at finding the grave cerements and corpse-like mask which they handled\",\n          \"position\": 13136,\n          \"confidence\": \"h