1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...s and folly, and made whispering vows, each to the other, that the next chiming of the clock should produce in them no similar emotion; and then, after the lapse of sixty minutes, (which embrace three thousa...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: vegetables (PROH-doos); to make (pruh-DOOS)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"word\": \"deliberate\",\n      \"flag_reason\": \"homograph\",\n      \"occurrences\": 1,\n      \"first_position\": 11611,\n      \"chapter_indices\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"context_examples\": [\n        \"...his group in the direction of the intruder, who, at the moment was also near at hand, and now, with deliberate and stately step, made closer approach to the speaker. But from a certain nameless awe with which t...\"\n      ],\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"ipa\": null,\n      \"phonetic_spelling\": null,\n      \"audio_url\": null,\n      \"user_pronunciation\": null,\n      \"notes\": \"Multiple pronunciations: adj (di-LIB-er-it); verb (di-LIB-er-ayt)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"glossary\": null,\n  \"overview\": {\n    \"structure\": {\n      \"chapter_count\": 1,\n      \"has_titles\": false,\n      \"has_parts\": false,\n      \"narrative_style\": \"unknown\",\n      \"description\": \"This book contains 1 chapters. Chapters are numbered sequentially.\"\n    },\n    \"plot_summary\": {\n      \"plot_summary\": \"The story begins in the grip of a merciless plague known as the Red Death, a disease that spreads with terrifying speed, marked by bleeding pores and vivid scarlet stains, driving society into isolation and despair. Amid this chaos, Prince Prospero, a man of extravagant tastes and unyielding pride, chooses defiance over surrender. He retreats with a thousand courtiers to his secluded, heavily fortified abbey, a fortress of luxury and distraction designed to shield them from the outside world’s suffering. Within the abbey’s impenetrable walls, they indulge in endless feasts, music, and revelry, attempting to drown out the dread beyond their gates. The prince, a figure of absolute authority and self-indulgence, becomes the central figure of this artificial sanctuary, his power and wealth symbolizing a desperate attempt to control fate.\\n\\nMonths pass in this suspended world of pleasure, until Prince Prospero hosts a grand masked ball in the abbey’s seven uniquely themed chambers, each adorned with stained-glass windows that cast colored light across the floor. The final chamber, however, is black—its walls draped in velvet, its windows blood-red, and dominated by a massive ebony clock that chimes each hour, halting all merriment with a chilling silence. The clock’s tolling serves as a grim reminder of time’s inevitability, instilling dread even in the most carefree guests. As the midnight chime echoes through the halls, a mysterious figure appears—dressed as the Red Death itself, its form drenched in blood and wearing a mask that resembles a corpse’s face. The guests are paralyzed with terror, unable to move or speak, as the figure glides through the rooms with unnatural grace.\\n\\nEnraged by the intrusion and the violation of his sanctuary, Prince Prospero draws a dagger and pursues the figure through the seven chambers, driven by fury and denial. His pursuit is a desperate act of rebellion against the very reality he has tried to escape. He finally confronts the figure in the black chamber, only to collapse and die instantly, his body succumbing to the plague he had so arrogantly denied. In that moment, the truth is revealed: the figure is not a guest, but the Red Death incarnate, the embodiment of the disease he had sought to outrun. As the clock chimes once more, the plague spreads through the abbey with terrifying speed, claiming every reveller in turn. Darkness and decay consume the once-luxurious halls, and the sanctuary of wealth and privilege collapses into a tomb of silence and rot, underscoring the futility of resisting fate.\",\n      \"themes\": [\n        \"identity\",\n        \"ambition\",\n        \"loss\"\n      ],\n      \"narrative_style\": \"first-person retrospective\"\n    },\n    \"model_usage\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3-next:80b-a3b-instruct-q8_0\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"model\": \"qwen3:30b-instruct\",\n        \"provider\": \"ollama\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"timing\": {\n      \"Chapter Detection\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 16.87,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"16.9s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Extraction\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 295.55,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"4m 56s\"\n      },\n      \"Chapter Summaries\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 24.38,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"24.4s\"\n      },\n      \"Character Profiles\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 19.55,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"19.6s\"\n      },\n      \"Pronunciation Guide\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 71.33,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"1m 11s\"\n      },\n      \"total\": {\n        \"duration_seconds\": 433.16,\n        \"duration_formatted\": \"7m 13s\"\n      },\n      \"started_at\": \"2026-01-19 00:52:49\",\n      \"ended_at\": \"2026-01-19 01:00:03\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"low_confidence_items\": [],\n  \"_analysis_metadata\": {\n    \"analyzed_at\": \"2026-01-19T01:0